WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.780
It didn't arrive. Should I just send a few more?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.136
Don't send again. Submitted, on-chain and credited are not the same thing.

00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:16.340
Find which station it's stuck at, then decide who to contact.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.494
Keep the send record.

00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:38.472
If there's a transaction hash, check it on a proper block explorer for that network:

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:43.450
status, destination address and amount. Don't mix in results from a different chain.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.112
The receiving platform may still need confirmations or an internal review.

00:01:04.112 --> 00:01:06.616
If the coin, network, address or memo was wrong,

00:01:06.616 --> 00:01:09.330
stop sending and give the facts to official support.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.445
A completed on-chain transfer usually can't be undone like a normal action.

00:01:28.445 --> 00:01:32.528
Whether it can be recovered depends on technical and platform conditions.

00:01:32.528 --> 00:01:33.703
There's no guarantee.

00:01:33.703 --> 00:01:37.450
Don't believe anyone who says paying a fee will surely get it back.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.620
Give the records they need. Never the recovery phrase, private key or codes.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.060
Right. Find where it's stuck first. Don't keep sending.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.910
'Hi, I'm support. Send me your recovery phrase. ' Next: what scammers really want.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.370
Understand first, then act.
